<title>RUSSIA: Russia's Sakhalin region plans Eurobond issue.</title>
<headline>Russia's Sakhalin region plans Eurobond issue.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sakhalin region, located in the Russian Far East, plans to issue a Eurobond in cooperation with AB Inkombank, the bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The bank declined to give any details.</p>
<p>Sakhalin joins a long queue of Russian regions, including Irkutsk, Nizhny Novgorod and Perm, which are issuing Eurobonds. The City of Moscow and St Petersburg have already successfully tapped international markets.</p>
<p>--Alexei Pankratov, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
